# NisPlayer marked a queued cinematic as started and reserved its arena space
# before opening the file. If DolphinFile's fixed 32-entry pool was temporarily
# full, nlOpen returned null but the loader passed it into AsyncManager and
# dereferenced it. Merely dropping that async read would also strand the queue
# in its started state forever.
#
# Open the file before changing either piece of queue bookkeeping. A failed
# open now leaves the request pending, so HandleAsyncs retries it on a later
# frame after older asynchronous reads have released their file handles.
